    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-11" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:EC.REG.715-2007" id="0">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">cites</data>
      <data key="d73">Regulation (EC) No 715/2007</data>
      <data key="d74">The technical requirements for the type-approval of motor vehicles, engines and replacement parts with regard to emissions are currently set out in two Regulations that apply to emission type-approval for light-duty and heavy-duty vehicles respectively, namely Regulation (EC) No 715/2007 of the European Parliament and of the Council (9) and Regulation (EC) No 595/2009 of the European Parliament an</data>
      <data key="d75">direct</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-11" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:EC.REG.715-2007" id="1">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">cites</data>
      <data key="d73">Regulation (EC) No 715/2007</data>
      <data key="d74">Regulation (EC) No 715/2007 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 20 June 2007 on type approval of motor vehicles with respect to emissions from light passenger and commercial vehicles (Euro 5 and Euro 6) (OJ L 171, 29.6.2007, p. 1).</data>
      <data key="d75">footnote</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-11" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:EC.REG.715-2007" id="2">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">amends</data>
      <data key="d73">Regulation (EC) No 715/2007</data>
      <data key="d74">Regulation (EC) No 595/2009 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 18 June 2009 on type-approval of motor vehicles and engines with respect to emissions from heavy duty vehicles (Euro VI) and amending Regulation (EC) No 715/2007 and Directive 2007/46/EC and repealing Directives 80/1269/EEC, 2005/55/EC and 2005/78/EC (OJ L 188, 18.7.2009, p. 1).</data>
      <data key="d75">footnote</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-11" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:EC.REG.595-2009" id="0">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">cites</data>
      <data key="d73">Regulation (EC) No 595/2009</data>
      <data key="d74">The technical requirements for the type-approval of motor vehicles, engines and replacement parts with regard to emissions are currently set out in two Regulations that apply to emission type-approval for light-duty and heavy-duty vehicles respectively, namely Regulation (EC) No 715/2007 of the European Parliament and of the Council (9) and Regulation (EC) No 595/2009 of the European Parliament an</data>
      <data key="d75">direct</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-11" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:EC.REG.595-2009" id="1">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">cites</data>
      <data key="d73">Regulation (EC) No 595/2009</data>
      <data key="d74">Regulation (EC) No 595/2009 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 18 June 2009 on type-approval of motor vehicles and engines with respect to emissions from heavy duty vehicles (Euro VI) and amending Regulation (EC) No 715/2007 and Directive 2007/46/EC and repealing Directives 80/1269/EEC, 2005/55/EC and 2005/78/EC (OJ L 188, 18.7.2009, p. 1).</data>
      <data key="d75">footnote</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-11" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:EC.DIR.2007-46" id="0">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">amends</data>
      <data key="d73">Directive 2007/46/EC</data>
      <data key="d74">Regulation (EC) No 595/2009 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 18 June 2009 on type-approval of motor vehicles and engines with respect to emissions from heavy duty vehicles (Euro VI) and amending Regulation (EC) No 715/2007 and Directive 2007/46/EC and repealing Directives 80/1269/EEC, 2005/55/EC and 2005/78/EC (OJ L 188, 18.7.2009, p. 1).</data>
      <data key="d75">footnote</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-11" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:EC.DIR.1980-1269" id="0">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">amends</data>
      <data key="d73">Directives 80/1269/EEC</data>
      <data key="d74">Regulation (EC) No 595/2009 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 18 June 2009 on type-approval of motor vehicles and engines with respect to emissions from heavy duty vehicles (Euro VI) and amending Regulation (EC) No 715/2007 and Directive 2007/46/EC and repealing Directives 80/1269/EEC, 2005/55/EC and 2005/78/EC (OJ L 188, 18.7.2009, p. 1).</data>
      <data key="d75">footnote</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-12" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:EC.REG.715-2007" id="0">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">cites</data>
      <data key="d73">Regulations (EC) No 715/2007</data>
      <data key="d74">Incorporating the requirements laid down in Regulations (EC) No 715/2007 and (EC) Nó 595/2009 into a single Regulation would ensure internal coherence of the system of emission type-approvals for both light and heavy-duty vehicles, while allowing for different emission limits and testing procedures for such vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d75">direct</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-14" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:UNGTR-15" id="0">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">cites</data>
      <data key="d73">UN Global Technical Regulation No 15</data>
      <data key="d74">Considering that existing technologies and the UN Global Technical Regulation No 15 allow the measurement of particle number emissions down to 10 nanometres (PN10), it is appropriate to apply the particle limits to PN10 for all vehicles covered by this Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d75">direct</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-17" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:EC.REG.715-2007" id="0">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">cites</data>
      <data key="d73">Regulations (EC) No 715/2007</data>
      <data key="d74">Regulations (EC) No 715/2007 and (EC) No 595/2009 require that vehicles respect the emission limits for a specified period of time, which does not correspond to the average lifetime of vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d75">direct</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EU2024-1257.RECITAL-17" target="EU2024-1257/EXT:EC.REG.595-2009" id="0">
      <data key="d71">CITES</data>
      <data key="d72">cites</data>
      <data key="d73">(EC) No 595/2009</data>
      <data key="d74">Regulations (EC) No 715/2007 and (EC) No 595/2009 require that vehicles respect the emission limits for a specified period of time, which does not correspond to the average lifetime of vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d75">direct</data>
    </edge>
